   "date": "1939",
   "from": "",
   "to": "Department of State",
   "about": "Assesses Japan’s capacity to sustain gold exports and expand production while maintaining currency reserves.",
   "summary": "The report compares gold shipments with reserves taken over by the government and doubts that exports near their 1937–1938 levels can continue. It surveys gold output in Japan, Taiwan, Korea, and Manchukuo, including mining interests, foreign concessions, equipment shortages, and ambitious production targets. It describes subsidies, refining plans, restrictions on gold use, a census of private holdings, and possible compulsory sales. The closing pages list attachments, distribution, sources, and related reports.",
